        <briefdescription>
<para>Detect reversed &quot;0 op variable&quot; patterns and derive sign properties. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>When exact zero appears on the left and a variable on the right, the operator semantics are reversed to derive the variable&apos;s sign:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>0 LT var → var is Positive (0 &lt; var means var &gt; 0)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>0 GT var → var is Negative (0 &gt; var means var &lt; 0)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>0 GEQ var → var is NonPositive (0 &gt;= var means var &lt;= 0)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>0 LEQ var → var is NonNegative (0 &lt;= var means var &gt;= 0)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>0 NEQ var → var is NonZero</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
